{"documentId":"tos.work.friedrich-nietzsche.also-sprach-zarathustra","versionId":"gutenberg-1998-common-en","revision":"0854ebabe235d46c8e5e099418c5189b1df0848898c552009b70d924b9065d05","units":[{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-fc7b40b31e494b9ca2474788fdaca1a6","ordinal":2921,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2921","text":"2.\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-51b1512c5a2246928b27e900cf972f20","ordinal":2922,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2922","text":"Then did Life answer me thus, and kept thereby her fine ears closed:\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-87b7a0ae4f7c431b871c95ba06dd537e","ordinal":2923,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2923","text":"“O Zarathustra! Crack not so terribly with thy whip! Thou knowest surely\r\nthat noise killeth thought,—and just now there came to me such delicate\r\nthoughts.\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-c0dcd9493b364c57adab9c1e9d09cde7","ordinal":2924,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2924","text":"We are both of us genuine ne’er-do-wells and ne’er-do-ills. Beyond\r\ngood and evil found we our island and our green meadow—we two alone!\r\nTherefore must we be friendly to each other!\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-ce30ffa42141417fa78dc1b68714a26b","ordinal":2925,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2925","text":"And even should we not love each other from the bottom of our\r\nhearts,—must we then have a grudge against each other if we do not love\r\neach other perfectly?\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-12ab2b343aa8416bad2842e29069f101","ordinal":2926,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2926","text":"And that I am friendly to thee, and often too friendly, that knowest\r\nthou: and the reason is that I am envious of thy Wisdom. Ah, this mad\r\nold fool, Wisdom!\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-8a87a7c09f164d00b22345ea7bee552a","ordinal":2927,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2927","text":"If thy Wisdom should one day run away from thee, ah! then would also my\r\nlove run away from thee quickly.”—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-96dc594e23d645378aee3db4ab8937a4","ordinal":2928,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2928","text":"Thereupon did Life look thoughtfully behind and around, and said softly:\r\n“O Zarathustra, thou art not faithful enough to me!\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-d20582ebc4774397aee292dc7740d7c5","ordinal":2929,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2929","text":"Thou lovest me not nearly so much as thou sayest; I know thou thinkest\r\nof soon leaving me.\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-d15a72ab2e1f43b1b1d739331310c306","ordinal":2930,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2930","text":"There is an old heavy, heavy, booming-clock: it boometh by night up to\r\nthy cave:—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-fd123a1dd2964b07a687c46fdace6fd8","ordinal":2931,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2931","text":"—When thou hearest this clock strike the hours at midnight, then\r\nthinkest thou between one and twelve thereon—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-e120d1bcfe15402bb33bc223118c49e5","ordinal":2932,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2932","text":"—Thou thinkest thereon, O Zarathustra, I know it—of soon leaving\r\nme!”—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-f93a8a9d37b54b61820ea8b5f8ab49bb","ordinal":2933,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2933","text":"“Yea,” answered I, hesitatingly, “but thou knowest it also”—And I\r\nsaid something into her ear, in amongst her confused, yellow, foolish\r\ntresses.\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-90628806d8734263863bb4a8811dd8a5","ordinal":2934,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2934","text":"“Thou KNOWEST that, O Zarathustra? That knoweth no one—”\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-9a4261f51ea24afe836581ec5a865d36","ordinal":2935,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2935","text":"And we gazed at each other, and looked at the green meadow o’er which\r\nthe cool evening was just passing, and we wept together.—Then, however,\r\nwas Life dearer unto me than all my Wisdom had ever been.—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-d7ed92a506f54e20aa4ef6f6d311aefd","ordinal":2936,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2936","text":"Thus spake Zarathustra.\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-56eb320ba61d4b1dacef5d4bc387a720","ordinal":2937,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2937","text":"3.\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-871926b31a6d4cc19cf7a9b6d1809adb","ordinal":2938,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2938","text":"_One!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-609392c1c11e47f2b8781dcf732185f6","ordinal":2939,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2939","text":"O man! Take heed!\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-f80a63574849465c8e549add17a94055","ordinal":2940,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2940","text":"_Two!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-2602bf66a72f4302837e28efeec3885c","ordinal":2941,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2941","text":"What saith deep midnight’s voice indeed?\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-b67f28d93d8a434d885c3dfa54d89741","ordinal":2942,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2942","text":"_Three!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-57f88de675b8435193c9cd21051a97e3","ordinal":2943,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2943","text":"“I slept my sleep—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-48c7f0086efe4cd196a4be3c3187e60f","ordinal":2944,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2944","text":"_Four!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-c326b52d9eba4fa9ba934af7b1dcedbe","ordinal":2945,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2945","text":"“From deepest dream I’ve woke and plead:—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-9bfa7b6b365c4751b1c359485ab71d28","ordinal":2946,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2946","text":"_Five!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-837bb79b2e5645baa011cd1664148bcf","ordinal":2947,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2947","text":"“The world is deep,\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-04721a26d01b463cacad67315b739dfd","ordinal":2948,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2948","text":"_Six!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-5bdb2918610e4ccc9c17eb29d4c2c6bd","ordinal":2949,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2949","text":"“And deeper than the day could read.\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-9559b761238142b3a471c0a9c1ede00f","ordinal":2950,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2950","text":"_Seven!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-46a6f9fe16f747d2a37db544b0634e9a","ordinal":2951,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2951","text":"“Deep is its woe—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-f90ab799cb6d4d6183926bda83bcd563","ordinal":2952,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2952","text":"_Eight!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-d4c50e8dc29c42f287e0c0a158516456","ordinal":2953,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2953","text":"“Joy—deeper still than grief can be:\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-f8d7b678df8743acbe4055d4f717f9d6","ordinal":2954,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2954","text":"_Nine!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-e5e0ddf6385740d2a91ef3e1b3a99056","ordinal":2955,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2955","text":"“Woe saith: Hence! Go!\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-b5b80f4e27104281be5d5e137c4684fc","ordinal":2956,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2956","text":"_Ten!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-7d7ef631efe649988fbd4d5efd56b3a1","ordinal":2957,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2957","text":"“But joys all want eternity—\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-3e72ad82073b40c59497bb3f07783edc","ordinal":2958,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2958","text":"_Eleven!_\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-8d7625776cd74d78b91a86634d0f2211","ordinal":2959,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2959","text":"“Want deep profound eternity!”\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"tos.text-unit.sid-0cee424bf9f240858e152752ae383bac","ordinal":2960,"kind":"paragraph","language":"en","reference":"Unit 2960","text":"_Twelve!_\r\n\r\n"}]}